From a0a73c630c8d94929392f53ce24018185b353007 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:21:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 82/85] hw/gpio: MCP23017/MCP23S17 I/O expander core, MCP23017,
 Expand 2 Click

Mcp23x17 holds what the two parts share (DS20001952D section 3): both
register layouts (IOCON.BANK), byte and sequential addressing with the
A/B toggle, pads from OLAT, external drivers and the 100 kOhm pull-ups,
IPOL, interrupt on change against the previous value or DEFVAL with
INTF and INTCAP (cleared by reading GPIO or INTCAP), INTA/INTB with
MIRROR, ODR and INTPOL, RESET#. The bus side calls mcp23x17_read() and
mcp23x17_write(); a callback reports the pads.

"mchp-mcp23017" puts it on I2C; GPA7 and GPB7 are outputs only on
the MCP23017 (revision D, 3.5.1), so IODIR written with IO7 set logs
a guest error (they still work as inputs). QOM: "levels", "drive" and "pa0".."pb7"
(a pad held to ground, for the Expand 2 Click's headers on the page).

Expand 2 Click v100: 0x20 (A2..A0 on ground), INTA on INT (J2), RESET#
on RST without a pull resistor.

qtests: registers, pull-ups, IPOL, outputs, both interrupt modes, BANK
1 and RESET# on the MC00's EXT1; a pad read through TWI0 on the
AVR64EA48 Nano Base.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
